UID:370bdb1ac0cb19e35147641b0305a2e8@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nCelebrate Indigenous People&#8217
 \;s Day with Journeys to the Past\, presented by Segerstrom Center for t
 he Arts. Through storytelling\, songs\, traditional instruments\, and han
 ds-on cultural objects\, families will learn about Native American history
 \, traditions\, and the importance of preserving Indigenous cultures.\nTim
 es: 11am and 2:30pm\nSpace is limited! Book your tickets now\; this prog
 ram is included in museum admission.\nDisclaimer: *Events and dates are su
 bject to change. \nAbout the partner: Continuing the tradition of his mot
 her Jacque Nunez\, Jackson Rolling Thunder and family bring to life Native
  American culture and history as they share their people’s tools\, games
 \, clothing\, stories\, instruments and songs. \n&nbsp\;\\n\\nMore info
 : https://www.pretendcity.org/events/celebrating-indigenous-peoples-day/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/celebrating-indigenous-peoples-day/
