SUMMARY:Dia de Los Muertos in the City
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T110000
DTSTAMP:20261009T150405Z
UID:07e2a5f3df749a09280a2d3210d61b1d@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nCome celebrate Dia de Los Muertos 
 with us! Sing along to Flower Songs Music\, decorate a sugar skull\, and e
 njoy a live Folklorico performance. It&#8217\;s a day to remember loved on
 es and celebrate life through color\, music\, and tradition.\nTimes:\n11am
  &#8211\; Flower Songs Music present by Segerstrom Center for the Arts\n12
 pm-2pm &#8211\; Sugar Skull Decorating Drop In\n2:30pm &#8211\; Folklorico
  with Relámpago del Cielo\nSpace is limited! Book your tickets now\; this
  program is included in museum admission.\nDisclaimer: Events and dates ar
 e subject to change. \nAbout the play partners:\nFlower Songs Music share
 s culture\, history\, instruments\, and songs in English\, Spanish\, and n
 ative languages. This family of musicians\, poets\, researchers\, and educ
 ators\, aim to share their rich culture while fostering community and incl
 usivity.\nArts Teach is an education program by Segerstrom Center for the 
 Arts that offers assembly performances and workshops in Dance\, Music\, Th
 eater\, and Visual Arts for schools and community organizations. \nRelám
 pago del Cielo \nRelámpago del Cielo\, Inc. Grupo Folklórico celebrates
  45 years in Santa Ana as the oldest operating non-profit institution of i
 ts kind within the region and the largest in the United States. \nOver th
 e years\, RDC has touched the lives of generations in the community\, offe
 ring low-cost Mexican Folkloric dance classes for all ages\, dance recital
 s\, and special performances locally and internationally.\n&nbsp\;\n&nbsp
 \;\n&nbsp\;\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/dia-de-los-
 muertos-in-the-city/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/dia-de-los-muertos-in-the-city/
